Description: skip dh_doxygen under nodoc profile
 libevdev's `debian/rules` `override_dh_installdocs-indep` runs:
 .
   dh_installdocs -i
   dh_doxygen -i -plibevdev-doc
 .
 The second line installs the doxygen-generated HTML reference into
 the `libevdev-doc` binary package.  Under
 `DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc` (Athena's default — `[Source]
 BuildProfiles = nodoc, nocheck` in build.conf), the upstream
 `dh_auto_build-indep -Bdoc` step doesn't actually run the doxygen
 generator, so there's no HTML output for `dh_doxygen` to find:
 .
   dh_doxygen: error: Doxygen documentation not found
   make[1]: *** [debian/rules:45: override_dh_installdocs-indep] Error 25
 .
 Drop the `dh_doxygen` invocation entirely.  Under nodoc this is the
 right behaviour — there's nothing to install.  The `libevdev-doc`
 binary package still gets built (it's an arch-indep .deb that ships
 README + changelog via `dh_installdocs` above), it just won't carry
 the doxygen HTML reference under our build profile.
 .
 The trade-off: a hypothetical full (non-nodoc) build would also stop
 shipping the doxygen HTML.  We never run a full build (nodoc is
 hard-coded for Athena), so this is acceptable.  If a future Athena
 variant needs doxygen output, gate the line on the inverse of
 `nodoc` instead of removing it outright.
 .
 Surfaced during GROUPS-01 phase 3 gnome build 2026-05-14 — libevdev
 is pulled in transitively as a Build-Depends of mutter (gnome-shell's
 compositor) for input-event handling.
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-15
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -42,4 +42,3 @@

 override_dh_installdocs-indep:
 	dh_installdocs -i
-	dh_doxygen -i -plibevdev-doc
